# SATUSEHAT-4D — Multi-Branch Readiness Scale-Up & Operational Governance

1. SATUSEHAT-2 remains WATCH; its GO tag remains absent. SATUSEHAT-4D is
   credential-independent: no OAuth / sandbox / production / external FHIR HTTP.
2. SATUSEHAT-4D GO covers **internal** multi-branch readiness + operational
   governance only. It does NOT mean SATUSEHAT-2 GO, external submission,
   production activation, or Kemkes acceptance.
3. Multi-branch operations include only RME-enabled branches. MAIN is excluded
   (enforced via `BranchService::rmeEnabledIds()` in the service layer).
4. No rollout wave is active by default (starts `draft`). No branch is a pilot
   by default. Branch enrollment requires an explicit, audited action.
5. A branch may belong to only ONE active wave (service check + partial unique
   index `trx_ss_wave_membership_active_uq`).
6. Branch promotion requires every INTERNAL hard gate to pass and ZERO open hard
   blockers. A high readiness score can never override a hard blocker. Demotion
   occurs when hard readiness regresses (a known trigger from config).
7. The external credential blocker is ALWAYS a separate, ever-present signal;
   every matrix row shows `blocked_external_credential`.
8. Threshold/scoring-weight/wave-membership/pilot/suspension/terminology/rollout
   changes go through change-control. `production_guard_config` and
   `credential_state` categories can be logged but can NEVER be approved/applied
   during 4D. Requester != approver (separation of duties).
9. Human operator UAT sign-off is MANDATORY for an operational GO. Automated
   tests never substitute. A UAT run reaches `signed_off` only when every
   required role approves and no scenario failed. UAT evidence is synthetic /
   PII-safe. Operator names/sign-offs are never fabricated.
10. Admin Klinik is branch-pinned (matrix read + own-branch remediation only).
    Owner is read-only aggregate (matrix + executive). Kasir and Admin Lab are
    denied. No role gains external-send or production permission.
11. No remote identifier (Organization/Location/Patient/Practitioner IHS) may be
    fabricated. NIK/KTP and raw clinical notes are never rendered or exported;
    executive/owner views are aggregate-by-default.
12. No auto-send. No Send-All. Bulk issue operations are bounded (paginated
    selection only, MAX_BULK), server-side branch-scoped, and never bulk-resolve
    HARD issues.
13. Multi-branch synthetic rehearsal is marker-scoped, network-silent, and ends
    honestly at `BLOCKED_EXTERNAL_CREDENTIAL` (or `INCOMPLETE`) — never
    `submitted`/`external_success`. A failed branch is isolated from the others.
14. Production remains blocked. The primary health endpoints remain healthy while
    SATUSEHAT is disabled. Deployment runner executes only on the VPS. Nginx
    `listen 80 default_server;` protection and the AishPOS co-tenant must not
    regress.
15. Migrations are additive only (`migrate` — never `migrate:fresh`/`db:wipe`).
    Append-only tables (score snapshots, transitions, drill runs, audit) are
    never mutated in place.
16. External GO requires the SATUSEHAT-2 External Credential Closure Campaign.
